4. FALSE-ADMISSION RISK OF EACH CANDIDATE GATE
====================================================================================================
   An A/A null compares identical code to itself, so EVERY failure here is a false
   REJECTION and every pass is correct-by-construction. The risk a wider band carries is
   that it also admits a REAL position effect. Priced by asking what each band would have
   admitted across every null measured above.

