====================================================================================================
5. THE FIX, AND ITS WIN/LOSE SPLIT (gate-fix evidence standard)
====================================================================================================
   change: the A/A null's halves become FIRST WARM vs LAST, i.e. slot 1 vs slot 3 at
   round_warmup=0 and slot 0 vs slot 3 above it. NO STANDING MOVES — the quoted ratio is
   still the median over all four slots; only which slots the NULL compares changes.

   band                        old halves {s0,s1}/{s2,s3}    first-warm vs last
   +/-0.02 (enforced)                              83.3%                 54.2%
   0.97-1.03 (bead's)                              70.8%                 33.3%
   +/-0.05                                         64.6%                 20.8%
   +/-0.10                                         50.0%                  4.2%

   Every rejection above is a FALSE rejection: an A/A null compares identical code to
   itself, so there is no true positive to trade away. The false-ADMISSION risk of the fix
   is that a genuine early-vs-late position effect now has 2 samples behind it instead of
   4, widening the null's own CI — which the existing MAX_NULL_CI_WIDTH=0.60 limb catches
   as WIDE rather than admitting. The band is NOT widened, so no real effect of size >2%
   becomes admissible that was not already.
